## Third-party components

Murmur installs and calls the following at runtime. Their licences apply to
them, not to Murmur, and none of their code is vendored into this repository.

- **faster-whisper** (MIT) and **CTranslate2** (MIT) — CPU transcription.
- **mlx-whisper** (MIT) — Apple Silicon GPU transcription.
- **OpenAI Whisper models** (MIT) — the speech models themselves, downloaded
  on first run.
- **whisper.cpp / ggml** (MIT) — optional alternative backend. If you
  distribute the ggml model files under `bench/models/`, the MIT attribution
  requirement travels with them.
- **pynput** (LGPL-3.0) — global hotkey capture. Used as an unmodified
  library via its public API; not linked statically, not modified.
- **sounddevice** (MIT) and **PortAudio** (MIT) — audio capture.
- **pyobjc** (MIT) — macOS system integration.
- **anthropic** (MIT) — optional cleanup client.
- **rumps** (BSD-3-Clause) — optional menu-bar companion.

Speech audio is processed entirely on the local machine. When an Anthropic API
key is configured, transcribed **text** — never audio — is sent to the
Anthropic API under that key holder's own account and terms.
